// src/pages/commercial/ice-machines/manitowoc-error-codes.astro
// Wave 70 Phase 2b Batch 17 — Manitowoc error codes REFERENCE page (70 vol/mo).
// Encyclopedia-style reference for Manitowoc Indigo NXT named alerts + Q-Series
// legacy codes. Builds on canary 346b820 + post-P0-hotfix brands/manitowoc.astro
// + error-codes.astro authoritative table.
// FOCUS: deep-dive on 6 Indigo NXT named alerts + Fault History menu navigation +
// reset procedure. Q-Series legacy mentioned generically (no fake specifics per
// P0 hotfix lesson).
// $120 commercial. BHGS #A49573 + EPA 608 Universal #1346255700410.

import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CommercialHero from '../../../components/CommercialHero.astro';
import { MAIN_PHONE } from '../../../data/branches';
import { BRANCH_LOCATIONS_GEO_NEUTRAL } from '../../../lib/build-location-array';

const phone = MAIN_PHONE;
const phoneRaw = MAIN_PHONE.replace(/\D/g, '');
const phoneHref = `tel:+1${phoneRaw}`;
const canonical = "https://samedayappliance.repair/commercial/ice-machines/manitowoc-error-codes/";

const title = "Manitowoc Error Codes Reference LA — Same Day";
const description = "Manitowoc error codes reference — Indigo NXT touchscreen named alerts + Q-Series numeric legacy + Fault History menu. LA same-day. BHGS #A49573.";

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "What does Long Freeze mean on my Manitowoc?",
    a: "Long Freeze on a Manitowoc Indigo NXT touchscreen means the freeze cycle exceeded its design time. The cycle timer fired without the cell sensor reaching the freeze-complete signal. Three usual causes in order of frequency: refrigerant under-charge or condenser fouling (sealed-system side — EPA 608 work to confirm), water inlet valve partial restriction reducing fill speed, or ambient temperature exceeding the unit's spec (kitchen heat above 90°F during LA summer service triggers the protection). Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair check head pressure on manifold gauges and inspect the condenser fins first because that resolves the majority of Long Freeze calls. Typical resolution $245 to $385 condenser cleaning or $700 to $1,500 refrigerant work."
  },
  {
    q: "What does No Harvest mean on my Manitowoc?",
    a: "No Harvest on an Indigo NXT touchscreen means the freeze cycle completed but ice didn't release from the evaporator during the harvest cycle. Three usual causes: the harvest assist mechanism is stuck or worn (most common on year-5+ IY/IB cubers), the Acu-Thaw hot gas valve failed to open and warm the evaporator, or the water curtain switch isn't reading the expected open/closed state during the cycle. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair inspect the harvest assembly and curtain switch first because those resolve roughly 6 of every 10 No Harvest calls. Acu-Thaw hot gas valve replacement $340 to $540 if that turns out to be the failure."
  },
  {
    q: "What does Curtain Switch alert mean?",
    a: "Curtain Switch on an Indigo NXT means the water curtain wasn't detected closed or open at the expected time in the freeze and harvest cycle. The curtain is the hinged flap that closes the freeze chamber during ice formation and opens during harvest; the switch reads its position. Causes: the curtain itself is warped or stuck, the switch is misaligned or failed, or there's a wiring fault between switch and control board. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair check curtain alignment first because that's free to rule out — switch replacement runs $185 to $285 if the mechanical inspection clears."
  },
  {
    q: "What does High Discharge Temp mean on my Manitowoc?",
    a: "High Discharge Temp on an Indigo NXT touchscreen means the compressor discharge temperature exceeded safe operating range. The control board cuts power to protect the compressor from further damage. Three usual causes: condenser fouling restricting heat rejection (most common, $245 to $385 cleaning resolves), condenser fan motor failure on -A air-cooled units (high-pitched whine or no airflow, $300 to $520 motor replacement), or refrigerant over-charge from prior service work. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair check condenser fin condition and fan operation first because those resolve the majority of High Discharge Temp calls — and on tight kitchen installations the cause is often inadequate clearance for airflow rather than a component failure."
  },
  {
    q: "What does Low Water alert mean on my Manitowoc?",
    a: "Low Water on an Indigo NXT means insufficient water at the freeze chamber for the freeze cycle to complete. Three usual causes in order of frequency: water supply shut off or partially closed at the wall valve (free to check), water filter cartridge clogged (Pentair Everpure or 3M Cuno on most Manitowoc installs, 6-month replacement cycle), or the water inlet valve has failed closed. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair check the supply valve and filter first because those resolve roughly 4 of every 10 Low Water calls at no parts cost. Water inlet valve replacement runs $260 to $420 if the upstream supply side checks clean."
  },
  {
    q: "What does Bin Full alert mean on my Manitowoc?",
    a: "Bin Full on an Indigo NXT touchscreen means the bin-fullness sensor reports the bin is full and the machine has stopped production accordingly. Two scenarios: (1) Legitimate full bin — sensor is correct, empty the bin and production resumes automatically. (2) Sensor fault — the bin is empty but the sensor is misreading; empty the bin completely and observe whether production resumes. If yes, sensor is failing — replacement $180 to $280. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair note whether Bin Full is intermittent (sensor drift, usually replace) or persistent (often legitimate full or wiring fault) by reading the Fault History menu first."
  },
  {
    q: "How do I navigate the Indigo NXT Fault History menu?",
    a: "Fault History is in the Service menu on the touchscreen home screen — navigate to Service then Fault History. The display shows the most recent alerts with timestamps, allowing intermittent-vs-recurring distinction. Steady-state alerts (same alert repeating every cycle) usually point to a hard component failure. Intermittent alerts (same code appearing then clearing) often point to upstream conditions (water pressure dip, ambient spike, brief power blip). Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair read the Fault History first on every visit because that pattern often points at different parts than the active alert alone would suggest."
  },
  {
    q: "How do I reset my Manitowoc Indigo NXT?",
    a: "Indigo NXT resets through the touchscreen menu: navigate to Service then Reset Faults from the home screen. If the underlying fault is still present, the alert returns within minutes, and the Fault History preserves the record. On older Q-Series legacy machines without touchscreen, reset is a power-cycle at the breaker (wait 60 seconds, restore power). Resetting without diagnosing is fine as a temporary workaround while you wait for our visit; don't ignore an alert that keeps returning. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair always read Fault History before resetting so the diagnostic trail is preserved."
  },
  {
    q: "How long does Manitowoc error-code-related repair take?",
    a: "Repair time depends on which alert and what component fails. Long Freeze + High Discharge Temp from condenser fouling: 60 to 90 minutes cleaning, same-day. Low Water from water inlet valve: 60 to 90 minutes, same-day. No Harvest from Acu-Thaw hot gas valve: 90 to 120 minutes, same-day. Curtain Switch replacement: 60 to 90 minutes, same-day. Bin Full from sensor: 45 to 75 minutes, same-day. Long Freeze from refrigerant leak (EPA 608): 3 to 5 hours including leak detection plus evacuation plus recharge. Easy-Read display board: same-day if on truck (2 to 3 hours); otherwise 1 to 3 day Welbilt expedite. Common Indigo NXT parts (water inlet valves, harvest sensors, curtain switches, fan motors) are stocked on the van for first-visit completion."
  },
  {
    q: "How much does Manitowoc error-code-related repair cost?",
    a: "Diagnostic visit + Fault History menu read $120, waived with repair. Typical repair ranges by alert: Long Freeze (condenser cleaning $245-$385 or refrigerant work $700-$1,500); No Harvest (Acu-Thaw valve $340-$540 or harvest sensor $200-$340); Curtain Switch (switch $185-$285); High Discharge Temp (condenser cleaning $245-$385 or fan motor $300-$520); Low Water (water inlet valve $260-$420 or filter $80-$180); Bin Full (sensor $180-$280). Most named-alert calls resolve in the $200 to $540 range when the alert points to water-side or sensor work. Refrigerant-related alerts (Long Freeze from leak, High Discharge Temp from sealed-system) run higher, $700-$1,500 EPA 608 work."
  },
  {
    q: "How can I prevent Manitowoc error codes?",
    a: "Three preventive practices reduce error-code frequency significantly. (1) Maintain 2 to 4 cleanings per year with Manitowoc Cleen Ice brand-spec cleaner — scale buildup triggers Long Freeze, High Discharge Temp, and Low Water alerts on Indigo NXT vertical evaporator. (2) Replace water filter cartridges on the 6-month schedule (Pentair Everpure or 3M Cuno) — overdue filters trigger Low Water and accelerate water inlet valve wear. (3) Inspect condenser fin clearance quarterly and clean the fins during scheduled service — fouled condenser is the single biggest cause of Long Freeze and High Discharge Temp alerts. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair offer quarterly contract service with documented LA County DPH compliance — typically $720 to $1,200 annual for cleaning + filter replacement + condenser cleaning."
  }
];

